      "raw_text": "To determine how many potted plants Mary will remain with, let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of plants Mary currently has.**\nMary already has plants on 40 window ledges, with 2 plants on each ledge.\n$$40 \\text{ ledges} \\times 2 \\text{ plants/ledge} = 80 \\text{ plants}$$\n\n**Step 2: Add the new plants she received.**\nShe received 18 new potted plants from the nursery.\n$$80 \\text{ existing plants} + 18 \\text{ new plants} = 98 \\text{ total plants}$$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the number of plants she gives away.**\nShe decides to give 1 plant from each of the 40 window ledges to friends and family.\n$$40 \\text{ ledges} \\times 1 \\text{ plant/ledge} = 40 \\text{ plants given away}$$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the remaining number of plants.**\nSubtract the plants given away from the total number of plants.\n$$98 \\text{ total plants} - 40 \\text{ plants given away} = 58 \\text{ plants remaining}$$\n\nAlternatively, we can think of it this way:\nShe starts with 80 plants. She adds 18, making 98. She removes 40.\n$98 - 40 = 58$.\n\n#### 58<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To determine how many potted plants Mary will remain with, let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of plants Mary currently has.**\nMary already has plants on 40 window ledges, with 2 plants on each ledge.\n$$40 \\text{ ledges} \\times 2 \\text{ plants/ledge} = 80 \\text{ plants}$$\n\n**Step 2: Add the new plants she received.**\nShe received 18 new potted plants from the nursery.\n$$80 \\text{ existing plants} + 18 \\text{ new plants} = 98 \\text{ total plants}$$\n\n**Step 3: Calculate the number of plants she gives away.**\nShe decides to give 1 plant from each of the 40 window ledges to friends and family.\n$$40 \\text{ ledges} \\times 1 \\text{ plant/ledge} = 40 \\text{ plants given away}$$\n\n**Step 4: Calculate the remaining number of plants.**\nSubtract the plants given away from the total number of plants.\n$$98 \\text{ total plants} - 40 \\text{ plants given away} = 58 \\text{ plants remaining}$$\n\nAlternatively, we can think of it this way:\nShe starts with 80 plants. She adds 18, making 98. She removes 40.\n$98 - 40 = 58$.\n\n#### 58",
